# The sandbox at its default size, digging wooden planks apart. Once the
# sand and the water have fallen, it drops three 60 x 6 planks: onto the
# floor, onto the sand heap on the left ledge, where it rests tilted, and
# into the water on the right ledge, where it sinks onto the ledge. Then
# it digs through the middle of each, which breaks it in two bodies: the
# pieces on the sand heap slide off it. It digs a corner off a piece on
# the floor, then the rest of that piece and of one beside it into small
# bodies, and one of those away whole, which removes its body.
